    "body": "Research facts, from a read of `main` and a local read of the file. The file is not copied, and nothing of it is quoted here.\n\n**The check**\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_trims.rs:40`: `MAX_EDGE_GAP_MM = 0.01`. The gap is the largest distance from the 3D edge to the face surface, at 20 samples (lines 197-201). The refusal is at lines 205-210.\n- An accepted gap makes the edge tolerance and the vertex tolerance larger: 3 times the gap (lines 211-222).\n\n**The file**\n\n- The file states an uncertainty of 0.01 mm. That is equal to the cap. The measured gap of 0.0102 mm is 2 percent over it.\n- Face #230 is a B-spline surface. Its edge is a circle of radius 9 mm, by the edge order of the file. The edge order of the kernel can be different: not checked.\n- No code on `main` reads the uncertainty of a file. The solidcore units module calculates it, and the kernel does not use it.\n\n**What the previous reader did (v0.24.0)**\n\n- It had no cap for each edge against its surface. It used a seam gap of 2 times the chord, and a jump limit of 1e-3 mm for a boundary point. It did not read the uncertainty of the file.\n\n**The pins**\n\n- The smallest gap that a test refuses is 0.25 mm (`bspline_discontinuous.step`, `crates/app/tests/import_step_guard_default_cap.rs:45`).\n- The largest accepted gap on record is 1.2e-6 mm (`bar_cross_holes.step`, `docs/decisions/917-kernel-pcurves.md`).\n- No test has a gap between 0.01 mm and 0.25 mm.\n\n**After an accepted gap**\n\n- The mesh deviation check runs separately at the chord tolerance (`crates/kernel/src/machining_mesh.rs:312-341`). The reduced-fidelity flag depends on the chord, not on the edge gap.\n\n**Options for the work** (the worker measures the gap of each tracked fixture and of the maintainer's models first, then decides and records):\n\n- A: a larger fixed cap.\n- B: a cap from the uncertainty that the file states, with an upper limit.\n- C: accept to a second limit, and mark the model with a reduced-fidelity note that gives the measured gap.\n- D: keep the refusal.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
