    "body": "Measurement (issue-worker-max, 2026-11-20). A local harness that is not committed read each file with `read_step`. It printed the gap of each bare edge, as `cover_gaps` computes it (`GapFunction::crv_srf`, 20 samples). For this run, the 0.01 mm cap was off. The stated uncertainty comes from `solidcore_step::units::context`, in mm.\n\n| File | Stated uncertainty (mm) | Bare edges measured | Largest gap (mm) | > 0.001 | > 0.005 | > 0.01 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Lobe.step (private) | 0.01 | 28 | 1.015e-2 | 14 | 10 | 1 |\n| fig8.step | 0.01 | 1 | 3.5e-12 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| fillet_corner.step | 1e-6 | 2 | 8.2e-13 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| bar_cross_holes.step | 2e-5 | 4 | 1.19e-6 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| bspline_discontinuous.step | 1e-6 | 3 | 0.25 | 3 | 3 | 3 |\n| twisted_flank.step | 1e-6 | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| Milling-test.step | 0.01 | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| Milling-test-inch.step | 0.01 (inch file, converted) | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| sample_ap214.step | 1e-14 | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| box, bspline_dome, empty_list, spline_revolved, lathe_holder_offset, modular_clamp_unit, modular_lathe_head, tool_csys_box_iso13399 | 1e-6 | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n\n`twisted_flank_off.step` is refused before the gap check, as before.\n\n**A second refusal is behind the first one.** With the edge-gap cap off, `Lobe.step` reads as 1 solid. The reader adds its own note: 7 edges with a closed-form pcurve lie up to 1.507e-2 mm off their surfaces. That is 1.5 times the stated uncertainty. Then the machining mesh refuses the solid:\n\n| Chord (mm) | Result of `machining_mesh` |\n|---|---|\n| 0.005 (the import chord, `CHORD_CAP`) | refused: face 1 capped at 9.874e-3 mm sag |\n| 0.01 | refused: face 1 capped at 1.476e-2 mm sag |\n| 0.0125 | refused: face 1 capped at 1.563e-2 mm sag |\n| 0.015 | refused: face 1 capped at 1.563e-2 mm sag |\n| 0.02 | meshed: 10640 triangles, deviation 1.947e-2 mm, volume 113192.5 mm3 |\n| 0.03 | meshed: 9366 triangles, deviation 2.974e-2 mm |\n\nExact kernel volume of the solid: 113295.5 mm3. Bounding box: about 43 x 43 x 120 mm.\n\n**Result.** A cap from the stated uncertainty does not open this file. The planner cannot mesh a face to the chord when the edges of the face lie farther off the surface than the chord. The import chord is 0.005 mm (`CHORD_CAP = DEV_TOL / 2`). Thus each edge gap over about 0.005 mm stops the import at the mesh, with any edge-gap cap. This is a safe refusal: the mesh law bounds the mesh against the surface.\n\nTo open `Lobe.step`, the mesh tolerance must follow the file too. For example: mesh at a chord of about 2 x the stated uncertainty, and set the reduced-fidelity flag (`coarse()`). That chord (0.02 mm) is coarser than the stock-simulation verdict tolerance (`DEV_TOL` = 0.01 mm). This is a decision for the maintainer. The worker stops here, as its brief says. No code is changed. The branch `issue/2976-edge-gap-cap` has no commits.\n",
