    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T14:52:17Z",
    "body": "The maintainer decided (2026-11-20): option A, reduced fidelity.\n\n- The edge cap is 2 times the uncertainty that the file states, with a hard upper limit of 0.02 mm.\n- The model is meshed at a tolerance of up to 2 times the stated uncertainty (0.02 mm for the reported file).\n- The model gets the reduced-fidelity flag that exists today, and a note in plain English. The note names the measured gap and the tolerance that the file states. Each check then judges against the coarser tolerance, as the flag does now for a coarse mesh.\n- A file that states no uncertainty keeps the cap of 0.01 mm and its refusal.\n- Tests pin a gap just under the cap and a gap just over the cap. The refusal at 0.25 mm stays.\n- The decision file and the PR body state the cost: 0.02 mm is coarser than the verdict tolerance of the stock simulation (`DEV_TOL`, 0.01 mm).\n\nThe label is `claimed` again. The worker continues when the build slot of this session is free. A test build for the maintainer follows the fix.\n",
